<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 8.957 percent at Monday's auction from 8.956 percent at the previous auction on June 9.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1,433.825 million pounds, replace bills worth 927.625 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 1.3 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):.</p>
<p>Maturity date: Dec 16, 1997 (Dec 9, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.957 percent (8.956)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,433.825 million (1,382.475 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,582.275 million (1,666.775 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.600-9.037 percent (8.500-9.031)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.600-10.200 percent (8.500-9.935)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 108 (91)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 120 (141)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
